# Movable HUD implementation checklist

Source proposal: [MovableHudProposal.md](MovableHudProposal.md)
Parent task: [project.todo](../project.todo), HUD Indicators.

## Goal and scope

Make registered HUD indicators and their groups movable through hover controls, with native position persistence and geometric snapping. Keep feature overlays/presentations responsible only for readings, measurements, visibility, and drawing. Reuse native HUD/dialog lifecycle, event routing, GUI bounds/scaling, and position storage.

Do not add a VE layout file, serializer, persistent docking graph, automatic regrouping by snapping, or an editor for hidden indicators. Do not rewrite feature registrations or duplicate overlay instances. Built-in placements remain defaults. All tasks below remain unchecked until their stated evidence is available; source/headless results do not establish live interaction quality.

## Assumptions and decisions to resolve

- Use the native titlebar with its native Fixed/Movable dropdown and the approved compact orange skin: 22 GUI units high with shared 14-point HUD text. Adapt hover visibility, content-origin persistence, and cancellation around the widget; do not substitute a direct mode-toggle interaction.
- Saved positions use native integer GUI-unit X/Y coordinates, not persisted screen-edge anchors or pivots. Position presence records individual detachment. Client settings apply across worlds.
- Begin with a 6-physical-pixel snap threshold and Shift bypass. Select and document the wider release threshold and deterministic candidate tie-breaking during snapping work.
- Resolve compact handle dimensions, title/menu presentation, and control-to-content origin mapping in the prototype; do not silently introduce resize, close-indicator, or docking behavior.
- Run build/test tools through subagents as required by repository instructions. Leave live acceptance to the user; do not launch the game automatically.

## Phase 1: Verify one movable group and the native titlebar adapter

Outcome: one existing group can demonstrate hover controls, native persisted dragging, and safe cancellation before individual movement or snapping is built.

- [x] Reconfirm the owning seams in `HudOverlayHost`, `HudOverlayHoverLabels`, `HudOverlaySession`, `HudOverlayGroupLayout`, and native titlebar/composer input routing.
  - [x] Identify how group placement previews enter layout without being overwritten by ordinary per-frame synchronization.
  - [x] Keep the prototype restricted to one existing group, without changing feature overlays or presentation classes.
- [x] Prototype a separate native control composition around `GuiElementDialogTitleBar`.
  - [x] Use a distinct stable VE dialog key and native Fixed/Movable behavior, restore, and release-time persistence.
  - [x] Gate rendering/hit testing to free-cursor hover or active interaction; respect foreground dialogs and global HUD visibility.
  - [x] Keep controls visible while moving from content onto the handle and throughout dragging; place controls above content or below it near the screen edge.
  - [x] Establish consistent control/content origin mapping so moving the handle below the content never changes the saved content position.
  - [x] Route only handle/active-drag input, continue outside initial bounds, and avoid the default dialog methods' whole-composer event consumption.
  - [x] Preserve content measurements, packing, sampling, and prepared artwork while controls appear or positions change.
  - [x] Paint the slim titlebar with radial-menu orange and normal HUD text; keep native menu/close hit geometry aligned with its glyphs.
  - [x] Show a translucent orange panel over exact hovered group bounds behind the content, and an unfilled orange bounds outline whenever the cursor is free and that group is Movable.
- [x] Verify cancellation restores starting placement without committing a position: Escape, cursor capture changes, GUI hiding, world exit, target removal, and loss of active interaction.
- [x] Record the adapter decision with source/headless evidence and user-run interaction evidence.
  - [x] Check native focus management with other dialogs open; `Focusable = false` alone is insufficient.
  - [x] Reuse the actual native titlebar and dropdown while retaining safe content dragging, cancellation, and `GetDialogPosition`/`SetDialogPosition` persistence.
  - [x] Remove the rejected adapter path and temporary prototype-only scaffolding once the retained approach is established.

Completion criteria:

- [x] The retained approach supports one group, native persistence across client restart, reachable hover controls, selective input, and cancellation without a separate persistence system.
- [x] The user has validated the prototype's hover/input behavior, including foreground windows, before expansion to individual containers and snapping.

Completion evidence:

- The retained one-group integration uses the actual native titlebar and Fixed/Movable dropdown with the approved compact orange skin. Separate control bounds preserve content measurements and packing; native settings store the content origin rather than the temporary above/below titlebar origin.
- Source and headless coverage verifies selective input, native dropdown navigation, foreground-window priority, reachable controls, cancellation without persistence, content-origin restoration, resource reuse, and lifecycle cleanup. Appearance is reviewed in game rather than asserted through visual presets.
- The final full suite passed 2,199/2,199 tests with no failures or skips. Receipt: `artifacts/test-results/visual-policy/visual-policy-full.trx` (repository-relative). Second review and the independent completion audit found no remaining required source defect.
- The user previously confirmed dragging and position persistence, and explicitly signed off this prototype by requesting that Phase 1 be marked complete on 2026-10-17. This records acceptance without attributing additional individual live-test observations to the user. No game was launched by the agent.

## Phase 2: Resolve persisted group positions through the shared runtime

Depends on Phase 1. Outcome: every registered group uses a consistent saved/default/preview position with existing packing and native scaling.

- [ ] Add focused position integration under `HudOverlays`, keeping file responsibilities separate and session/system composition thin.
  - [ ] Assign stable, distinct VE namespaced group and indicator keys without colliding with other dialogs.
  - [ ] Read native positions and map valid integer GUI-unit content origins through `HudOverlayPlacement`; missing entries retain registered defaults.
  - [ ] Make active drag preview override saved placement and registered defaults, with starting placement retained for cancellation.
  - [ ] Apply native coordinate rounding and screen clamping; preserve saved origin through size/style changes, subject to reachability.
- [ ] Integrate group placement resolution with `HudOverlaySession`, `HudOverlayGroupLayout`, and scheduler anchor availability.
  - [ ] Use the same effective placement for layout and availability; a moved screen-positioned group must not depend on its former native anchor.
  - [ ] Preserve internal group packing and update bounds/clips without refreshing readings or allocating feature artwork.
  - [ ] Retain saved overrides across unrelated configuration changes; use registered placement again only after reset.
- [ ] Generalize the retained hover/drag controls to registered groups and add group-default restoration via clearing their native position keys.
  - [ ] Keep input, control composition resources, and preview state owned by the shared host/session runtime and release them safely on teardown/rebinding.
- [ ] Add focused verification for key isolation, native position read/write/reset, preview precedence/cancellation, scaling, viewport/style changes, effective-anchor availability, and unchanged packing/content ownership.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] All registered groups can use persisted positions and reset to defaults without altering feature registrations or other dialogs' settings.
- [ ] Position-only movement neither resamples readings nor recreates feature presentations, and session replacement leaves no retained interaction resources.

## Phase 3: Add individual containers, detachment, and return to group

Depends on Phase 2. Outcome: each drawable indicator can move independently while its original group continues packing the remaining members.

- [ ] Resolve effective membership before packing: no individual position means registered group membership; a saved position means an independent container.
  - [ ] Reuse native bounds, measurement, clipping, and render dispatch for independent containers without duplicate registration, sampling, or resource ownership.
  - [ ] Adapt the layout boundary as needed so independent containers do not require rewriting `HudOverlayRegistration.GroupId`.
  - [ ] Share effective placement with scheduler availability so detached indicators survive loss of their former group anchor.
- [ ] Add separate indicator titlebar and group-grip target identities using existing drawable/clipped hover targeting.
  - [ ] Do not expose invisible targets for hidden, inapplicable, unprepared, or merely reserved slots; retain their persisted positions.
  - [ ] Keep transient controls out of content footprints, group packing, and feature drawing.
- [ ] Implement individual drag preview and commit/cancellation.
  - [ ] Temporarily detach during preview and close the original group's gap; successful release saves the individual position.
  - [ ] Cancellation restores previous placement and membership, including when an already detached indicator is dragged again.
  - [ ] Keep detached indicators independent when their original group is moved or reset.
- [ ] Implement “return to group” by clearing the individual key, and reset-all by clearing known VE group/indicator keys.
  - [ ] Repopulate/repack the original group immediately after reattachment.
  - [ ] Preserve unrelated dialog settings and saved entries for temporarily unavailable integrations.
- [ ] Verify group/individual combinations, reset actions, visibility transitions, registration removal, temporary anchor loss, size/style changes, and repeated session lifecycle cleanup.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Grouped, detached, and restored indicators draw and update exactly once with consistent geometry/availability and persistent membership semantics.
- [ ] Group and individual controls are distinct, reachably positioned, and do not change feature measurements or ordinary input outside their interactions.

## Phase 4: Add geometric snapping and alignment guides

Depends on Phase 3. Outcome: group and individual drag previews align precisely without introducing persistent docking relationships.

- [ ] Implement a geometry-only snap calculation receiving candidate/target rectangles and returning an adjusted rectangle plus guides.
  - [ ] Derive the unsnapped candidate from starting content bounds and total pointer delta; never feed snapped corrections back into the next delta.
  - [ ] Gather screen edges and nearby visible VE indicator/group measured bounds, excluding the target, group descendants, handles, shadows, and tooltips.
  - [ ] Consider matching edges, center lines, and adjacent edges separated by the normal group gap; reject distant perpendicular spans.
  - [ ] Use the initial 6-physical-pixel threshold at every GUI scale, a wider release threshold, and deterministic tie-breaking.
  - [ ] Allow Shift to bypass snapping using the unchanged unsnapped candidate.
- [ ] Apply snapping between pointer movement and effective layout preview; if using native titlebar release saving, apply the final position before it persists.
  - [ ] Reconcile screen clamping with the final rectangle and remove any guide whose claimed alignment no longer holds.
  - [ ] Ensure release persists the preview with native rounding and cancellation retains the original saved position.
  - [ ] Render guides through shared runtime controls without owning feature textures/state or affecting measurements.
  - [ ] Keep snapping positional only: no implicit regrouping or subsequent follow relationships.
- [ ] Verify screen/peer alignment, adjacency gaps, exclusions, locality, competing targets, hysteresis, Shift switching, scale conversion, long drags without accumulated error, and clamping near screen edges.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Individual and group previews snap predictably; guides match committed geometry and native persistence restores the committed position.
- [ ] Moving previously aligned items later does not create unrequested attachment behavior or alter group membership.

## Phase 5: Reconcile documentation and obtain final acceptance

Depends on Phase 4. Outcome: the complete shared behavior is documented, validated, and accepted without confusing headless checks with live interaction evidence.

- [ ] Update permanent `HudOverlays.md`, README usage, and localized control/menu labels to match the retained implementation, persistence/reset rules, and snapping behavior.
  - [ ] Describe current behavior without historical change logs or staging language; keep proposal/checklist cross-references coherent.
  - [ ] Remove remaining prototype scaffolding and obsolete input/layout paths; retain only the chosen titlebar/handle approach.
  - [ ] Check new classes/methods have required XML comments, nontrivial logic explanations, and visibility/family regions.
- [ ] Run repository build and appropriate focused/full tests through subagents; record commands/results and distinguish source, headless, and live evidence.
  - [ ] Review existing host, layout, scheduler, style, visibility-transition, and lifecycle coverage for regressions; do not infer visual acceptance from test passes.
  - [ ] Reconcile each proposal requirement against implementation and verification; review the final diff and linked documentation.
- [ ] Obtain user-run in-game acceptance for all indicator styles and registered groups.
  - [ ] Check free-cursor access, above/below titlebars at every edge, tiny indicator controls, and distinct group versus indicator actions.
  - [ ] Check foreground inventories/windows and focus, dragging outside initial bounds, no gameplay click-through during drag, and unaffected normal input elsewhere.
  - [ ] Check cancellation triggers, fade/collapse behavior, detachment/reattachment/reset, size/style/resolution changes, and world/session transitions.
  - [ ] Check snap locality, guides, jitter resistance, Shift bypass, integer-coordinate commit, and persistence across client restart.

## Final acceptance

- [ ] Every source-proposal requirement is implemented and verified, or an explicit change is reconciled with the user and proposal.
- [ ] Native position storage is the sole persistence mechanism; feature overlay/presentation ownership and normal passive HUD behavior remain intact.
- [ ] Required build/tests, documentation review, cleanup, and user-run interaction evidence are complete.
- [ ] Only after these gates pass, mark the parent movable-HUD task in `docs/project.todo` complete.
